        { q: "Solve by matrix method: x + y = 3, x - y = 1.", a: "Write A X = B with A = [[1, 1],[1, -1]], X = [x, y]^T, B = [3, 1]^T. det A = (1)(-1) - (1)(1) = -2. adj A = [[-1, -1],[-1, 1]]. A inverse = (1/-2)[[-1, -1],[-1, 1]] = [[1/2, 1/2],[1/2, -1/2]]. X = A inverse B = [ (1/2)(3)+(1/2)(1), (1/2)(3)+(-1/2)(1) ]^T = [2, 1]^T. Final answer: x = 2, y = 1." }
