        { q: "In triangle ABC, if a = 7, b = 8, c = 5, find angle C.", a: "By cosine rule cos C = (a^2 + b^2 - c^2)/(2ab) = (49 + 64 - 25)/(2*7*8) = 88/112 = 11/14. Hence C = cos^-1(11/14) approximately 38.2 degrees. Final answer: C = cos^-1(11/14) approximately 38 degrees 13 minutes." }
