        { q: "Find the separate equations of the lines given by x^2 - 5xy + 4y^2 = 0.", a: "Treat as quadratic; factor: x^2 - 5xy + 4y^2 = (x - y)(x - 4y) since (-y)(-4y)=4y^2 and -y-4y=-5y. So the lines are x - y = 0 and x - 4y = 0. Final answer: x - y = 0 and x - 4y = 0." }
