        { q: "Find the distance of the point (1, 2, 3) from the plane 2x - y + 2z + 3 = 0.", a: "Distance = |2*1 - 1*2 + 2*3 + 3| / sqrt(2^2 + (-1)^2 + 2^2) = |2 - 2 + 6 + 3| / sqrt(4+1+4) = |9| / 3 = 3. Final answer: 3 units." },
        { q: "Find the angle between the line (x-1)/2 = (y)/3 = (z+1)/6 and the plane 2x + y - z + 3 = 0.", a: "Line direction b = (2, 3, 6), plane normal n = (2, 1, -1). sin(theta) = |b . n| / (|b||n|) = |2*2 + 3*1 + 6*(-1)| / (sqrt(4+9+36) sqrt(4+1+1)) = |4 + 3 - 6| / (7 * sqrt(6)) = 1/(7 sqrt(6)). So theta = sin^-1(1/(7 sqrt(6))). Final answer: theta = sin^-1(1/(7 sqrt(6))) approximately 3.3 degrees." }
